Good: 4 failures total (one shown via "expected '' but got undefined" line for lastRequests test, plus the three others). All 4 new tests fail as expected except "falls through..." which already passes (still a valid regression guard).

Now implement the fixes (GREEN) in `js/aiTeammateTokenUsageReporter.js`:

**Fix 1 — thread 1**: Replace the regex-extraction with brace-balanced extraction + fall-through.

```javascript
function extractFaPayload(text) {
    var marker = text.indexOf('fa-tokens:');
    if (marker === -1) return null;
    var start = text.indexOf('{', marker);
    if (start === -1) return null;
    var depth = 0;
    var inString = false;
    var escaped = false;
    for (var i = start; i < text.length; i++) {
        var ch = text.charAt(i);
        if (inString) {
            if (escaped) { escaped = false; }
            else if (ch === '\\') { escaped = true; }
            else if (ch === '"') { inString = false; }
            continue;
        }
        if (ch === '"') { inString = true; }
        else if (ch === '{') { depth++; }
        else if (ch === '}') {
            depth--;
            if (depth === 0) return text.substring(start, i + 1);
        }
    }
    return null;
}
```

Then in parseTokensLine:

```javascript
var faPayload = extractFaPayload(text);
if (faPayload != null) {
    var payload = parseJson(faPayload, null);
    // Only consume the line as an fa ledger entry when the payload is a valid
    // object carrying token counts; otherwise fall through to the
    // CommandLineUtils parsing below so the line is not silently dropped.
    if (payload && typeof payload === 'object' &&
        (payload.input != null || payload.output != null || payload.cacheRead != null)) {
        return {
            readTokens: parseInt(payload.input, 10) || 0,
            ...
            faSegment: payload.segment == null ? null : parseInt(payload.segment, 10),
            rawTokensLine: text.trim()
        };
    }
```

Wait — one edge: `payload.segment == null ? null : parseInt(payload.segment, 10)` — if segment is "abc", parseInt → NaN. NaN != null is true so dedup key becomes 's1:NaN'. Edge case, acceptable, but I could guard: `var seg = parseInt(payload.segment, 10); faSegment: isNaN(seg) ? null : seg`. Cleaner. But then segment: 0 → parseInt → 0, isNaN(0) false → 0. Good. Let me do that.

**Fix 2 — thread 2**: in extractTokenUsage:

```javascript
if (tokens.faSessionId && tokens.faSegment != null) {
