{"content":"Fixed. The greedy `/fa-tokens:\s*(\{.*\})\s*$/` regex is replaced by `extractFaPayload()` — a balanced-brace, string- and escape-aware scanner — so a payload wrapped in a larger log line or followed by trailing text is located reliably. The line is only consumed as an fa ledger entry when the payload parses to an object with at least one token count; otherwise `parseTokensLine` falls through to the legacy `CommandLineUtils` parser instead of hard-returning `null`, so the line is no longer silently dropped.

Covered by two new tests (both RED before the fix): `fa-tokens line with trailing content still parses via brace-balanced payload` and `falls through to CommandLineUtils parsing when fa-tokens payload is malformed`. Full suite: 1588 passed / 0 failed.
","path":"outputs/review_replies/thread_1.md"}

{"content":"Fixed. `faSegment` now preserves absence: `parseInt(payload.segment, 10)` with `isNaN` → `null`, so a payload without `segment` is distinguishable from a legitimate `segment: 0` (which still yields `0`). The dedup in `extractTokenUsage` only applies when `tokens.faSessionId` is present **and** `tokens.faSegment != null`; segment-less lines are never deduped and no longer dropped as false "replays".

Covered by the new test `fa payloads without segment are not deduped together` (two segment-less lines for the same session both count; RED before the fix). Full suite: 1588 passed / 0 failed.
","path":"outputs/review_replies/thread_2.md"}

{"content":"Fixed. The badge class is now a whitelist: `estimated → src-est`, `reported → src-rep`, and any other value gets a new neutral `.src-unknown` style (light gray, dotted border) — so a typo'd or future source value is never rendered with the solid green "reported" styling. The value text is still rendered verbatim (escaped) inside the badge, and the `row-est` row tint still applies only to `estimated`.

Covered by the new test `renders unknown source values with a neutral badge instead of the reported styling` (asserts `src-badge src-unknown` present, `src-rep` and `row-est` absent for an unknown source; RED before the fix). Full suite: 1588 passed / 0 failed.
","path":"outputs/review_replies/thread_3.md"}

{"content":"Fixed — the guard is now pinned by tests. Added the exact scenario from the thread: a `Requests 99 (pro)` line followed by an fa line with `"requests":3` asserts `usage.requests === 3` (not 99 + 3) and `usage.attempts[0].requestTier === ''`. Also added the companion assertion: an fa line **without** `requests` yields `usage.requests === 0` and does not inherit the stale 99.

One small production clarification to make the assertion meaningful: fa samples now pin `requestTier: ''` / `requestDuration: ''` explicitly instead of leaving them `undefined` — the merge guard `if (tokens.requests == null && lastRequests)` itself is unchanged. New test: `does not merge stale lastRequests metadata into fa-tokens lines` (RED before the fix). Full suite: 1588 passed / 0 failed.
